# Frankenstein's Monster, the November head (ticket 45): a square grey-green head with a flat top under a slab of coarse black hair with a
# fringe of points, a heavy brow ridge over drooping lids and small eyes, a blunt nose, a flat stitched mouth line with square teeth, scars
# and cross stitches across the forehead and cheek, and a big steel bolt through each side of the jaw with a head and a washer.
# Frame (the soldier's head_top socket, ticket 43): the origin is the socket, 1.815 m over the soles; the head faces +Z, +Y is up. The
# size and the height come from the head part (content/parts/frankenstein_head.sdf): normalized to the common size, the chin 4 cm lower than
# phase 1's (at 1.525 m, over the neck's top at 1.569 whose stub is inside it). The head turns on the Head bone, 0.25 m under the origin.
# The eyes are the machines' eye part (eye_machine) at a little under half size, meshed once, used twice.
format 1

# No collider (the hit shape of the head is a number in the registry), and never culled before 200 m: the head is what reads at range
collider none
cull 200

Detail detail=0.641
    Part part=frankenstein_head
